{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, user 8, Ops, hours 06:00-14:00 CT) says his warehouse office desktop BL-DT-0108 won't connect to the network; shift starts within an hour. P2, user blocked. Checked: account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, VPN access true. Device BL-DT-0108 (Win 11 Pro desktop) shows OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-10-09 12:48 UTC, disk fine (78% free), no warnings. Found: no KB article covers a wired desktop with no network (KB-014 is Wi-Fi laptops only), so no documented Tier 1 fix. User asked to restart the PC, check the network cable at both ends, and see whether colleagues nearby are affected. Still needed: on-site or remote check of the cable, wall port and switch port in the warehouse office; check whether the outage is wider in the warehouse (if several people are blocked, raise to P1/P2 per KB-014); a loaner/alternate workstation if it can't be fixed before his shift.",
  "reason": "No KB covers a wired desktop network outage; device confirmed offline and user is blocked before shift"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for letting us know. I can see your warehouse office desktop is offline on our side, so I've sent your ticket to our Tier 2 network team as a priority so they can look at it before your shift. While you wait, a few quick things could get you going sooner: 1) Restart the desktop. 2) Make sure the network cable is plugged in firmly at the back of the PC and at the wall jack, and see if the little lights next to the cable port are on. 3) Check if anyone else nearby in the warehouse office has lost their network too. If they have, please reply and tell us, because that changes how urgent this is. If a restart or reseating the cable fixes it, just reply and we'll close the ticket. Otherwise Tier 2 will contact you soon.",
  "internal_note": "User 8 (James O'Connor) reports desktop BL-DT-0108 has no network. Account is active, not blocked, has VPN access, and shows no failed logins. The device is offline: last check-in was 2026-10-09 12:48 UTC, disk is healthy and there are no warnings. KB-014 only covers Wi-Fi on laptops, and no KB covers a wired desktop with no network, so per policy I escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) instead of troubleshooting from general knowledge. I gave the user basic steps (restart, reseat the cable, check whether colleagues are affected). If more people in the warehouse turn out to be down, raise the priority per KB-014. A loaner workstation may be needed if this isn't fixed before the 06:00 CT shift start.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
